“This topic is flagged because its calculated average is below the configured review threshold.”

Do not call a student weak, unintelligent, or unsuccessful.

A risk flag is a learning-support indicator, not a diagnosis or judgment.

If no assessment data exists for a topic, show “Insufficient data” rather than “Needs attention.”

